  "notes": "PARTIALLY PINNED. The PyPI closure is resolved: every wheel is named, sized and hashed from pypi.org, solved from the packages' own declarations for CPython 3.13 on Windows x86-64 by tools/pin_breeze_models.py, which refuses a closure whose pins contradict one another. Breeze's own code is pinned file by file at 6eba901d1845353802652c708a4740fdfc5baa75 from raw.githubusercontent.com, each with its size and SHA-256. torch 2.9.1 and torchaudio 2.9.1 are NOT PyPI wheels here: the CUDA 12.8 builds live only on download.pytorch.org, so each is a versioned resolve the installer answers against the publisher's own index on the user's machine, taking the cp313 win_amd64 wheel of exactly that version and the SHA-256 the index states; the machine that wrote this could not reach download.pytorch.org, so `python tools/pin_breeze_models.py --torch` on one that can turns the index's word into committed constants. Flash attention 2 is installed with the runtime, from the community wheel flash_attn-2.8.3+cu128torch2.9.1cxx11abiTRUE-cp313-cp313-win_amd64.whl (Wildminder/AI-windows-whl (github.com/wildminder/AI-windows-whl, wheels.json)), checked at install time against the digest its host states and recorded in voice/managed-breeze-models.local.json; `--flash-attn` records it here. The model is DECLARED BUT NOT HASHED: its repository and revision are written down, the installer lists the files from the hub's own tree at install time and checks every one against the digest the hub states (the LFS SHA-256, or the git blob id of a small file), and records them in voice/managed-breeze-models.local.json; `--model` on a machine that can reach huggingface.co commits them. Not installed, on purpose: gradio (qwen-tts's demo) and Breeze's HTTP server and tests (fastapi, uvicorn, python-multipart, pytest, ruff); runtime.excluded records each reason.",
